WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.607
Welcome to Module 9. Up to this point, you have already seen how retrieval augmented generation, or rag,

00:00:06.607 --> 00:00:11.732
can bring external evidence into a language model workflow.

00:00:11.732 --> 00:00:17.842
You have also worked with language models, tools, vector databases, and validation.

00:00:17.842 --> 00:00:23.913
Now we are going to connect those pieces and give the workflow more control over what happens next.

00:00:24.521 --> 00:00:26.348
The central idea is simple.

00:00:26.348 --> 00:00:30.873
Traditional rag usually retrieves once and then generates.

00:00:30.873 --> 00:00:38.648
Agentic rag can inspect what it retrieved, decide whether the evidence is enough, change the search if needed,

00:00:38.648 --> 00:00:44.063
call another approved tool, and stop when a clear condition is satisfied.

00:00:44.063 --> 00:00:47.098
We will also use a hands-on notebook.

00:00:47.098 --> 00:00:57.238
It includes a small local Q W E N model, Chroma, Lang Chain tools, Duck Duck Go search, and a custom Lang Graph agent.

00:00:57.238 --> 00:01:01.674
The core lab can run without a paid language model A P I key.

00:01:02.458 --> 00:01:09.570
As you work through the module, keep one question in mind: does this task genuinely need another decision,

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:12.965
or would a simpler fixed workflow be better?

00:01:12.965 --> 00:01:16.723
That question will help you design stronger projects later.
